# Critiq is the only app on this origin that routes on the path. The other five
# put their state in the query string (?run=, ?g=, ?mode=), so their URLs are
# always a real directory and the asset server resolves them with no help.
#
# Two things constrain what can be written here, and both were learned the hard
# way from a rejected deploy:
#
#   1. A rule whose target ends in `/index` or `/index.html` is REJECTED when the
#      source ends in `/*`. Not a warning and not conditional on html_handling —
#      workers-sdk rejects it outright, because html_handling would strip the
#      `/index.html` back off and re-trigger the same rule forever. So these
#      point at `/critiq/`, the directory, and never at the file inside it.
#
#   2. That target is only stable because html_handling is "force-trailing-slash",
#      which makes `/critiq/` the canonical spelling. Under the default
#      "auto-trailing-slash" the canonical form is `/critiq` and this target would
#      bounce through a 307 that rewrites the address bar — destroying the very
#      permalink the rule exists to serve.
#
# The rules are also deliberately narrow. `/critiq/*` would cover the built
# assets too, and whether a 200 rewrite outranks a real file is a question worth
# never having to ask; `/critiq/r/` and `/critiq/example` contain no files.
/critiq/example    /critiq/  200
/critiq/example/   /critiq/  200
/critiq/example/*  /critiq/  200
/critiq/r/*        /critiq/  200
